IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc3-disability-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-contributions`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 paragraphs 13 to 16: housing cost contributions. Tests of layer 1.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text).
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE IS WRITTEN HERE FROM THE TEXT, beside the assertion, before the file was run: none was copied from what the encoding printed.
-- Amounts are in pounds. The amount of each contribution is the text's 96.55 (para 14(1)).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers.

-- A person's payments with payment n received (1 care component of disability living allowance, 2 child disability payment, 3 Scottish adult disability living allowance, 4 attendance allowance,
-- 5 pension age disability payment, 6 personal independence payment daily living component, 7 adult disability payment); n = 0 gives none.
GIVEN i IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
      status IS A `Status of a disability payment`
GIVETH A `Status of a disability payment`
`uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` i n status MEANS
    IF i EQUALS n THEN status ELSE `neither received nor so entitled`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      status IS A `Status of a disability payment`
GIVETH A `Disability payments of a person`
`uc3 test — only payment n has the status` n status MEANS
    `Disability payments of a person` WITH
        `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 1 n status
        `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 2 n status
        `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 3 n status
        `attendance allowance` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 4 n status
        `pension age disability payment` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 5 n status
        `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 6 n status
        `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `uc3 test — the status of payment i when payment n has the status` 7 n status

-- A person to whom paragraph 15(2) may apply. which: 0 none of the limbs; 1 certified blind (both certificates); 2 certified severely sight impaired but not by a consultant ophthalmologist;
-- 3 receives payment 6 (personal independence payment); 4 entitled to payment 6 but not receiving it; 5 receives payment 2 (child disability payment, in list (ba)); 6 entitled to payment 2 but not receiving it.
GIVEN which IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Person to whom paragraph 15(2) may apply`
`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` which MEANS
    `Person to whom paragraph 15(2) may apply` WITH
        `sight certificate` IS `Sight certificate` WITH
            `certified as severely sight impaired or blind` IS (which EQUALS 1) OR (which EQUALS 2)
            `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist` IS which EQUALS 1
        payments IS IF which EQUALS 3 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 6 `received by the person` ELSE IF which EQUALS 4 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 6 `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it` ELSE IF which EQUALS 5 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 2 `received by the person` ELSE IF which EQUALS 6 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 2 `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it` ELSE `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 0 `received by the person`

-- Paragraph 15(2): (a) blind; (b) to (da) in receipt of one of the seven payments (the care component of child disability payment is (ba)); (e) entitled to one of six of them (not child disability payment) but not receiving it.
-- Expected: blind (both certificates) gives TRUE; severely sight impaired without a consultant ophthalmologist's certificate gives FALSE; receiving payment 6 gives TRUE; entitled to payment 6 but not receiving it gives TRUE;
-- receiving child disability payment gives TRUE (limb (ba)); entitled to child disability payment but not receiving it gives FALSE (limb (e) does not list it); none gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` 2) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` 4) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` 5) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` 6) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the person` (`uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` 0) EQUALS FALSE

-- A renter. basis: the claim basis; first and second: the which-codes of the renter and of the other joint renter.
GIVEN basis IS A `Claim basis`
      first IS A NUMBER
      second IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Renter who may be exempt from housing cost contributions`
`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` basis first second MEANS
    `Renter who may be exempt from housing cost contributions` WITH
        `claim basis` IS basis
        `the renter` IS `uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` first
        `the other joint renter` IS `uc3 test — a person who may be exempt` second
-- Paragraph 15(1): no deduction for a single renter to whom (2) applies, or for joint renters where at least one is such a person.
-- Expected: a single renter who is blind gives TRUE; a single renter with the other joint renter's facts (who is blind) set gives FALSE (the other is not a renter of a single claim);
-- joint renters where the first is exempt gives TRUE; where the second only is exempt gives TRUE; where neither is exempt gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(1) — no deduction is made because of the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 1 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(1) — no deduction is made because of the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 0 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(1) — no deduction is made because of the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `joint claimants` 1 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(1) — no deduction is made because of the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `joint claimants` 0 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 15(1) — no deduction is made because of the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `joint claimants` 0 0) EQUALS FALSE

-- A non-dependant. which: 0 an adult with none of the limbs; 1 under 21 (aged 20); 2 aged 21; 3 in receipt of state pension credit; 4 in receipt of payment 6; 5 entitled to payment 6 but not receiving it;
-- 6 receiving payment 2 (child disability payment, which paragraph 16(2) does not list); 7 in receipt of carer's allowance; 8 in receipt of carer support payment; 9 a prisoner (detained under a sentence);
-- 10 detained in hospital under the mental health Acts (not a prisoner); 11 responsible for a child under 5; 12 a member of the armed forces away on operations, a son of the renter, who resided with the renter and intends to return;
-- 13 as 12 but does not intend to return; 14 as 12 but not the renter's son or daughter.
GIVEN which IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Non-dependant who may be exempt from a deduction`
`uc3 test — a non-dependant` which MEANS
    `Non-dependant who may be exempt from a deduction` WITH
        `age in complete years` IS IF which EQUALS 1 THEN 20 ELSE 30
        `in receipt of state pension credit` IS which EQUALS 3
        payments IS IF which EQUALS 4 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 6 `received by the person` ELSE IF which EQUALS 5 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 6 `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it` ELSE IF which EQUALS 6 THEN `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 2 `received by the person` ELSE `uc3 test — only payment n has the status` 0 `received by the person`
        `in receipt of carer's allowance` IS which EQUALS 7
        `in receipt of carer support payment` IS which EQUALS 8
        detention IS Detention WITH
            `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS FALSE
            `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS (which EQUALS 9) OR (which EQUALS 10)
            `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS FALSE
            `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS which EQUALS 10
        `responsible for a child under 5 years old` IS which EQUALS 11
        `a member of the armed forces away on operations` IS (which EQUALS 12) OR (which EQUALS 13) OR (which EQUALS 14)
        `the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters` IS (which EQUALS 12) OR (which EQUALS 13)
        `resided with the renter or joint renters immediately before leaving to go on operations` IS (which EQUALS 12) OR (which EQUALS 13) OR (which EQUALS 14)
        `intends to return to reside with the renter or joint renters at the end of the operations` IS (which EQUALS 12) OR (which EQUALS 14)

-- Paragraph 16(2): (a) under 21; (b) state pension credit; (c) to (ea) the six payments; (f) entitled to one of them but not receiving it; (g) carer's allowance; (ga) carer support payment; (h) a prisoner; (i) responsible for a child under 5;
-- (j) a member of the armed forces away on operations who is the son or daughter of the renter and resided with them and intends to return.
-- Expected: 0 FALSE; 1 TRUE (20 is under 21); 2 FALSE (21 is not); 3 TRUE; 4 TRUE; 5 TRUE; 6 FALSE (child disability payment is not in 16(2)); 7 TRUE; 8 TRUE; 9 TRUE; 10 FALSE (detained in hospital is not a prisoner);
-- 11 TRUE; 12 TRUE; 13 FALSE (does not intend to return); 14 FALSE (not the renter's son or daughter).
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 2) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 3) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 4) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 5) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 6) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 7) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 8) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 9) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 10) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 11) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 12) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 13) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 16(2) — the sub-paragraph applies to the non-dependant` (`uc3 test — a non-dependant` 14) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraphs 13 and 14(1): one contribution for each non-dependant in the unit, none for an exempt renter (15) or an exempt non-dependant (16); each is 96.55.
-- Expected: three non-dependants, of whom one is 20 (exempt, limb (a)) and one receives carer's allowance (exempt, limb (g)), for an ordinary renter: 1 contribution, 96.55;
-- three ordinary non-dependants: 3 contributions, 289.65; none: 0; the same three for a blind single renter: 0 (paragraph 15); for joint renters of whom one receives payment 6: 0;
-- for joint renters of whom neither is exempt: 3.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 14(1) — the amount of each housing cost contribution` EQUALS 96.55
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 1, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 7) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the sum of the housing cost contributions` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 1, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 7) EQUALS 96.55
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 2) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the sum of the housing cost contributions` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 2) EQUALS 289.65
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 0 0) EMPTY EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `a single claimant` 1 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 2) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `joint claimants` 0 3) (LIST `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 2) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 13 — the number of housing cost contributions to be deducted` (`uc3 test — a renter who may be exempt` `joint claimants` 0 0) (LIST `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 0, `uc3 test — a non-dependant` 2) EQUALS 3

-- Paragraph 14(2) and (3): the deductions come after every other step; where the contributions exceed the amount, the amount is reduced to nil and no further reduction is made from the award.
-- Expected: 300 less 2 x 96.55 = 193.10 gives 106.90; 100 less 193.10 gives 0 (reduced to nil, 14(3)(a)); equal amounts give 0; no contributions leave the amount; the further reduction (14(3)(b)) is 0 in every case.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3)(a) — the amount after the housing cost contributions are deducted` 300 193.1 EQUALS 106.9
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3)(a) — the amount after the housing cost contributions are deducted` 100 193.1 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3)(a) — the amount after the housing cost contributions are deducted` 96.55 96.55 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 14(2) and (3)(a) — the amount after the housing cost contributions are deducted` 300 0 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 14(3)(b) — the further reduction of the award for housing cost contributions` 100 193.1 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 14(3)(b) — the further reduction of the award for housing cost contributions` 300 193.1 EQUALS 0
